2026-10-09T19:24:33.0846073Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0947779Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0957615Z [0m
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0958487Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0959399Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0959812Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0960595Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0961824Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0962386Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0962700Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0963382Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0963584Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0964121Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0964769Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0965303Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0965704Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0965893Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0966166Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0966470Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0966788Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0967243Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0967392Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0967528Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0967712Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0968116Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0968632Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0970329Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0970534Z I will:
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0970731Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0971083Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0972213Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0973038Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0973717Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0974166Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0974636Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0975347Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0976208Z    /root
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0986470Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T19:24:33.0987189Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1003920Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1004891Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1005380Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1010460Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1014523Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1027131Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1027906Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1038567Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1039270Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1040046Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1040395Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1040682Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1041092Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1041842Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1042620Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1042986Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1043164Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1043664Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1043948Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1044286Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1044866Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1045112Z 
2026-10-09T19:24:33.1045129Z 
